{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2242 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d9a4b1d9a662401b6795c76c79153f8401869b5613dbd3acd9827834054425fd" :edb/db-before-t 2241 :edb/db-after-t 2242 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535554 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:26:23.318Z" 13194139535554 true] [17592186197948 1100 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v)$, where\n\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$.\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n$AAAAAAA$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535554 false] [17592186197948 1100 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2 ,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067400/assets/94484d767cbf92566de8b73fdbd887ea2da85fbf1dd9f3daf9a0c9ea73608d4b.png)\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535554 true] [17592186197948 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D$, the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S} = \\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S = \\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2u, 0, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 2v, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 4uv⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) &= ⟨x + y, x - y, xyz⟩ \\mid _{x = u^{2}y = v^{2}z = 1} \\\\\n&= ⟨u^{2} + v^{2}, u^{2} - v^{2}, u^{2}v^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}) &= ⟨u^{2} + v^{2}, u^{2} - v^{2}, u^{2}v^{2}⟩ \\cdot ⟨0, 0, 4uv⟩ \\\\\n&= (u^{2} + v^{2}) \\cdot 0 + (u^{2} - v^{2}) \\cdot 0 + u^{2}v^{2} \\cdot 4uv \\\\\n&= 4u^{3}v^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(S)F \\cdot dS &= ∬_(D)F(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′})dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)4 u 3 v 3dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535554 false] [17592186197948 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,x-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=1} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535554 true] [17592186197950 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1.$" 13194139535554 true] [17592186197950 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n$\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1$." 13194139535554 false] [17592186197950 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D$, the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S} = \\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S = \\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1 + 2u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2, 1, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1 + 2u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 1,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 3, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) &= ⟨z, x, y⟩ \\mid _{x = 1 + 2u + vy = u + vz = u - v} \\\\\n&= ⟨u - v, 1 + 2u + v, u + v⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}) &= ⟨u - v, 1 + 2u + v, u + v⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - 2, 3, 1⟩ \\\\\n&= (u - v) \\cdot (-2) + (1 + 2u + v) \\cdot 3 + (u + v) \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&=-2u + 2v + 3 + 6u + 3v + u + v \\\\\n&= 5u + 6v + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(S)⟨z, x, y⟩ \\cdot dS &= ∬_(D)F(r(u, v)) \\cdot (r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′})dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)(5u + 6v + 3)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{1}(5u + 6v + 3)dvdu \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}[5uv + 3v^{2} + 3v]_{v = 0}^{v = 1}du \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(5u + 6)du \\\\\n&= [\\frac{5}{2}u^{2} + 6u]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 10 + 12 \\\\\n&= 22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535554 false] [17592186197950 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩|}_{x=1+2u+v\\,y=u+v\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (-2)+(1+2u+v)\\cdot 3+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+2v+3+6u+3v+u+v \\\\  & =5u+6v+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[5uv+3{v}^{2}+3v]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5u+6)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2}+6u]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10+12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535554 true] [17592186198305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354986 13194139535554 true] [17592186198305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354993 13194139535554 true] [17592186198305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355021 13194139535554 true] [17592186198305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355028 13194139535554 true] [17592186198307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355000 13194139535554 true] [17592186198307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355007 13194139535554 true] [17592186198307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355014 13194139535554 true] [17592186198512 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535554 true] [17592186198512 1100 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u, v)$, where\n\n$F(x, y, z) = ⟨2x + y, 2z, y + z⟩, r(u, v) = ⟨ - u^{2}, 2u^{2} - v^{2}, v^{2}⟩, (u, v) ∈ D⊂R^{2}$.\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$∬_(S)F \\cdot dS = ∬_(D)AAAAAAAdA$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} = ⟨8uv, 4uv, 4uv⟩$.*" 13194139535554 false] [17592186198512 1100 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" 13194139535554 true] [17592186198512 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535554 true] [17592186198513 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535554 true] [17592186198513 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-1,\\,2v,\\,2-3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" 13194139535554 true] [17592186198513 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$∬_(S)⟨3x + y + z, \\frac{y}{2} - 2,-3x - z⟩ \\cdot dS$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$r(u, v) = ⟨u - 1, 2v, 2 - 3u - 2v⟩$\n\nfor $-1 \\le u \\le 1$ and $0 \\le v \\le 3$." 13194139535554 false] [17592186198513 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩|}_{x=u-1\\,y=2v\\,z=2-3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3(u-1)+(2v)+(2-3u-2v),\\,\\frac{2v}{2}-2,\\,-3(u-1)-(2-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-1,\\,v-2,\\,2v+1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6+(v-2)\\cdot 2+(2v+1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6+2v-4+4v+2 \\\\  & =6v-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3x+y+z,\\,\\frac{y}{2}-2,\\,-3x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}(6v-8)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[u]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [3{v}^{2}-8v]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535554 true] [17592186198519 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535554 true] [17592186198519 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-1,\\,uv,\\,3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.$*" 13194139535554 true] [17592186198519 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$∬_(S)⟨2x, \\frac{xz}{3} - 2y, 2z⟩ \\cdot dS$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$r(u, v) = ⟨2u - 1, uv, 3v⟩$\n\nover the domain $D = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 1,-1 \\le v \\le 2}$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} = ⟨3v,-6, 2u⟩$.*" 13194139535554 false] [17592186198519 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$